  <h1>Wega Browser: Third-Party Notices</h1>
  <p>Wega is licensed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (see <code>LICENSE</code> and
  <code>NOTICE</code> shipped beside this file). It is built from the Rust crates listed
  below, each used under the license shown. Source for every crate is available from
  <a href="https://crates.io/">crates.io</a> or the linked repository; Wega's own source,
  including the modified Servo and epaint copies under <code>vendor/</code>, is at
  <a href="https://github.com/wulfnb/wega">github.com/wulfnb/wega</a>.</p>

  <h2>Bundled fonts</h2>
  <p>The user interface toolkit (egui, crate <code>epaint_default_fonts</code>) compiles
  these fonts into the executable. Their full license texts appear in the
  <code>epaint_default_fonts</code> entries below.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ubuntu Light</strong> (<code>Ubuntu-Light.ttf</code>): Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0.</li>
    <li><strong>Noto Emoji</strong> (<code>NotoEmoji-Regular.ttf</code>): SIL Open Font License 1.1.</li>
    <li><strong>Hack</strong> (<code>Hack-Regular.ttf</code>): MIT License (Copyright 2018 Source Foundry
      Authors); glyphs derived from Bitstream Vera under the Bitstream Vera License; DejaVu
      changes are in the public domain.</li>
    <li><strong>emoji-icon-font / egui-icons</strong>: MIT License (Copyright 2014 John Slegers).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Overview of licenses</h2>
  <ul>
    {{#each overview}}
    <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
    {{/each}}
  </ul>

